-- title:
--   Level-one Deuring correspondence with Brandt matrices
-- statement:
--   Let $q'$ be a prime and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q'$ which is an algebraic $\mathbb{F}_{q'}$-algebra. Let $X_0$ be an elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ all of whose points $P$ with $q'\cdot P=0$ vanish, and let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt`: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the completion $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $\Lambda\subset\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an order (containing $1$, multiplicatively closed, of full $\mathbb{Q}$-span, finitely generated) and maximal among orders containing it, and let $\theta$ be an injective ring homomorphism from `rationalEndSubring` $\kappa\,X_0$ — the subring of $\operatorname{End}$ of the points of the base change generated by the rationally represented additive maps — into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with range exactly $\Lambda$. Assume the class set $\mathrm{ClassSet}$ of the stabiliser of the finite adelic box of $\Lambda$, that is the double coset quotient of $(\mathbb{H}\otimes\mathbb{A}_f)^\times$ by the diagonal image of $\mathbb{H}^\times$ and that stabiliser, and the set $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q'\,1\,\kappa$ of rational affine geometric places $w$ of the level-one modular function field with $w(j)\in\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q'\,\kappa$, are both finite. Then there is a bijection $\Phi_1$ from the class set to $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q'\,1\,\kappa$ with two properties. First, for every unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_f$ and every elliptic Weierstrass curve $W$ over $\kappa$ whose $j$-invariant is the value of `jGeomGen` at the place $\Phi_1([x])$: there are a nonzero $\chi$ in `rationalHomSet` $\kappa\,X_0\,W$ and a unit $d$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ such that $\theta$ carries the kernel ideal $\{\rho\circ\chi:\rho\in\mathrm{rationalHomSet}\,\kappa\,W\,X_0\}$ onto the quaternion conjugate of $d\cdot(\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda})$, and moreover there is an injective ring homomorphism from `rationalEndSubring` $\kappa\,W$ to $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with range $\mathbb{H}\cap x\widehat{\Lambda}x^{-1}$. Second, for every prime $\ell\neq q'$, given integrality of the two degeneracy maps `heckeAlphaC` $\kappa\,1\,\ell$ and `heckeBetaC` $\kappa\,1\,\ell$ into the roof field and classes $i,j$, the supersingular Hecke matrix entry `ssHeckeMatrixC` $q'\,\kappa\,1\,\ell$ at $(\Phi_1 i,\Phi_1 j)$ — the sum over places of the roof restricting to $\Phi_1 j$ along $\beta$ and to $\Phi_1 i$ along $\alpha$ of the ramification index along $\beta$ times the inertia degree along $\alpha$ — equals the entry at $(i,j)$ of `classSetHeckeMatrix` for the stabiliser of $\Lambda$ and the set `primeHeckeSet` $\Lambda\,\ell$, namely the Hecke kernel count at $(j,i)$.
--
--   This is the level-one Deuring correspondence in Waterhouse's kernel-ideal formulation, together with the identification of the supersingular Hecke (Brandt) matrices at primes $\ell\neq q'$ on the two sides; Deuring's embedding of the endomorphism ring of the fixed supersingular curve onto a maximal order is taken as the hypothesis $\theta$. It is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_supersingular_rationalEndSubring_range_eq_of_isMaximalOrder`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_supersingular_rationalEndSubring_range_eq_of_isMaximalOrder), and thus feeds the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison between the supersingular points of the modular curve in characteristic $q'$ and the class set of a definite quaternion order.
